0,Languages of Africa - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Languages_of_Africa,"The Niger–Kordofanian language family, joining Niger–Congo with the Kordofanian languages of south-central Sudan, was proposed in the 1950s by Joseph Greenberg. Today, linguists often use ""Niger–Congo"" to refer to this entire family, including Kordofanian as a subfamily.",Nambya,Niger-Congo
